# --- Analysis data (root rule) ---
# Raw RVV CSVs aren't redistributable; .ics + external API fetches re-fetchable;
# built parquet regenerable via `uv run python pipeline/...`.
# Layout + how to rebuild: analysis/data/README.md
analysis/data/**
# ...but keep folder skeleton + README so teammates see the layout:
!analysis/data/
!analysis/data/**/
!analysis/data/**/README.md
!analysis/data/**/.gitkeep
# ...and keep MANUAL research output (NOT regenerable — written by research
# agents with per-row source URLs; grouped under raw/crawled/. See
# analysis/docs/EVENTS.md, STRIKES.md):
!analysis/data/raw/crawled/events_regensburg_2024_2025.csv
!analysis/data/raw/crawled/strikes_rvv_2024_2025.csv
# ...and the Betriebskalender extract (98 rows hand-pulled from the 3 SMO
# Betriebskalender PDFs — not regenerable without re-reading them; see
# analysis/docs/BETRIEBSKALENDER.md):
!analysis/data/raw/crawled/betriebskalender_events.csv
# ...and keep OTH semester .ics (tiny text; re-fetchable but OTH pulls old
# semesters — fetch_university_calendar.py needs them as a stable fallback):
!analysis/data/raw/oth_ics/*.ics
# ...and keep the committed GTFS snapshot (~86 KB; bbox-filtered extract of the
# 245 MB gtfs.de Germany feed — saves teammates the re-download. See
# analysis/docs/GTFS.md). stops_geo.parquet is derived from this + the RVV
# window parquets, so it stays gitignored like every other data/parquet/ output.
!analysis/data/raw/gtfs/regensburg_stops.parquet
# ...and the GTFS text inputs the RVV-native matcher reads (stop_code → DHID →
# coords). July is the city feed (stops + line numbers); aug backfills coords.
# Tiny text (~50 + ~190 KB) — committed so teammates rebuild with no download.
# The big stop_times/trips/calendar files stay ignored. See analysis/docs/GTFS.md.
!analysis/data/raw/gtfs_july2025/stops.txt
!analysis/data/raw/gtfs_july2025/routes.txt
!analysis/data/raw/gtfs_aug2025/stops.txt
# ...and the small RVV/SMO reference docs from the data bundle (text PDFs +
# stop/zone masters, all <350 KB, useful + not regenerable). What each is and
# what it's good for: analysis/docs/RAW_INPUTS.md.
!analysis/data/raw/2023_SMO_Betriebskalender.pdf
!analysis/data/raw/2024_SMO_Betriebskalender.pdf
!analysis/data/raw/2025 - SMO-Betriebskalender.pdf
!analysis/data/raw/Linien_Erklärung.pdf
!analysis/data/raw/Haltestellen und -punkte - Haltestelle.csv
# Regensburg census zones (473 polygons, residents by age group). City open
# data — license unverified, fine for the hackathon; recheck before any public release.
!analysis/data/raw/Population_Regensburg_2023/**

# --- Python ---
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/

# --- Jupyter ---
# Notebooks themselves stay tracked (committed with outputs — see analysis/README.md).
# Ignore the auto-saved checkpoints JupyterLab drops next to every open notebook.
.ipynb_checkpoints/
*-checkpoint.ipynb

# --- Secrets ---
.env
.env.local
.env.*.local

# --- Editor / OS ---
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo
